    "summaryAr": "About the Role You’ll grow Daybreak revenue across the Americas by helping partners sell our cybersecurity products and build services around them. You’ll teach their teams when a product like Daybreak Defense Factory fits the customer’s needs and when it makes sense to build something of their own with our models and tools. This is a hands-on partner sales role spanning global system integrators (GSIs), managed secu",
    "descriptionAr": "About the Role You’ll grow Daybreak revenue across the Americas by helping partners sell our cybersecurity products and build services around them. You’ll teach their teams when a product like Daybreak Defense Factory fits the customer’s needs and when it makes sense to build something of their own with our models and tools. This is a hands-on partner sales role spanning global system integrators (GSIs), managed security service providers (MSSPs), hyperscalers, security independent software vendors (ISVs), and value-added resellers (VARs). You’ll develop partner capabilities for your assigned territory or portfolio and work alongside partner sellers and OpenAI account teams to sell joint solutions and expand customer adoption. In this role, you will: Own commercial results. Grow revenue through partner relationships. Build qualified pipeline, progress opportunities, and support sustained customer use and expansion. Maintain accurate opportunity records and a disciplined forecast. Build cyber practices with partners. Work with partner executives and technical teams to turn customer demand into commercially viable cybersecurity offerings. Help partners establish the service economics, practitioner capacity, and delivery quality needed to build a repeatable business. Lead the partner side of customer deals. Help partner sellers scope what they’ll sell and deliver. Work with OpenAI account teams from discovery and customer business cases through evaluation, procurement, and close. Coordinate co-sell, marketplace, and channel activity, address buying and delivery barriers, and help customers move into deployment. Develop partner champions. Build trusted relationships with executive sponsors, security practice leaders, technical champions, and field sellers. Equip them to explain the customer value, identify opportunities, and sell and deliver supported AI-enabled security solutions. Turn cyber and AI use cases into credible offers. Explore how AI can support customer needs in areas such as vulnerability assessment, application security, and remediation. Work with specialists to validate capabilities, security outcomes, and delivery readiness before making commitments. Improve execution with evidence. Use what you learn from customer evaluations and deployments to improve offerings. Bring recurring needs and practical lessons to OpenAI’s product, technical, and go-to-market teams. How you’ll work You’ll own the cyber business in your territory or portfolio. Where an alliance lead owns the broader partner plan, you’ll lead the cyber part of it. You’ll work with OpenAI account teams on deals and bring in Partner Engineering to validate what we can deliver before the partner commits. You might thrive in this role if you have: A record of delivering revenue through enterprise partner sales, alliances, or business development in cybersecurity, cloud, or AI, including personally progressing complex customer opportunities. Strong partner business acumen and experience building repeatable offerings. You understand how services firms, managed security providers, cloud providers, security software companies, and resellers invest, make money, and mobilize their sellers and practitioners. Deep experience in at least one area of security, such as application security, red teaming, or security operations. You’ve used AI in that work and can explain to a CISO why it matters. You can teach a practitioner how the model, harness, and plugin work together and what data and permissions the tools need. Experience helping enterprise customers adopt a new product while its market was still forming. The ability to earn trust with partner executives and champions while working effectively with account teams, alliance leaders, technical teams, Product, and Marketing. Strong account planning, opportunity management, and forecasting skills, with the judgment and persistence to build a business in a developing market. Deeper familiarity with how a model and its harness work together, including how the surrounding software supplies tools and context and enforces permissions. Preferred experience Experience working as a security practitioner or sales engineer, or selling AI or developer tools to technical buyers. What success looks like: Revenue growth supported by qualified pipeline, healthy conversion, and accurate forecasting. Partner sellers can scope and win the next deal, and their practitioners can deliver the service profitably with less help from OpenAI. Customer deployments that progress to sustained use, expansion, and demonstrable security outcomes. About OpenAI OpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity. We are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. For additional information, please see OpenAI’s Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement . Background checks for applicants will be administered in accordance with applicable law, and qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment consistent with those laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act, for US-based candidates. For unincorporated Los Angeles County workers: we reasonably believe that criminal history may have a direct",
