    "summaryAr": "Camunda is the enterprise platform for agentic orchestration , enabling organizations to coordinate AI agents, people, and systems across complex, end-to-end business processes. With built-in governance, auditability, and human oversight, Camunda gives enterprises the control they need to move AI from pilots to production — safely and at scale. Trusted by over 700 organizations worldwide , including 9 of top 10 US ba",
    "descriptionAr": "Camunda is the enterprise platform for agentic orchestration , enabling organizations to coordinate AI agents, people, and systems across complex, end-to-end business processes. With built-in governance, auditability, and human oversight, Camunda gives enterprises the control they need to move AI from pilots to production — safely and at scale. Trusted by over 700 organizations worldwide , including 9 of top 10 US banks, Camunda helps enterprises boost operational efficiency, accelerate time-to-value, and deliver better customer experiences. Fully remote and global, we are in the middle of something bigger: transforming into an AI-first organisation, built on our own platform . We use Agentic AI to automate, orchestrate intelligent processes, and elevate human contribution across every team. Named GP Bullhound’s Top 100 Next Unicorn list, 2025 Great Place to Work certified. Visionary in 2025 Gartner® Magic Quadrant™ for Business Orchestration and Automation Technologies. ranked 3rd in Flexa's 2026 Most Flexible Companies , We’re growing fast and looking for top talent to join our team. If you want meaningful work, visible impact and put something genuinely rare on your CV, keep reading. About the Role: You’ll build the operating engine that helps our team turn global campaigns into regional pipeline for EMEA and LATAM. Sitting between global strategy and regional execution, you’ll adapt enterprise messaging and resources for regional buyers, then run, automate, and improve the work behind them: campaign setup, intake, localization, reporting, and follow-up. This is a hands-on role. Roughly half your time goes to running regional activation and operations well. The other half goes to automating, templating, and improving that work as a core part of how the team operates. You will work closely with the Global Integrated Campaigns team, Field Marketing, Marketing Ops, EMEA/LATAM sales leadership, ADRs, Product Marketing & Partner Marketing. What you'll be doing: Regional activation and localization Serve as the primary EMEA point of contact for the Growth Marketing teams (integrated campaigns, ABM, etc.), localizing company-wide programs for each sub-region and owning the regional campaign execution plan: goals, messaging angles, channel mix, and asset translation, all within brand standards. Help activate ADRs and Sales on localized campaigns. Campaign and program execution Lead end-to-end local delivery across digital, email, social and ABM and collaborate with Field marketing on relevant industry events that are part of the overall campaigns. Manage timelines, vendors, and multi-channel coordination to hit regional pipeline targets. Build and launch campaigns and events hands-on in HubSpot (emails, landing pages, forms, lists, workflows) and Salesforce (campaign build-out, list pulls, segmentation), to Marketing Ops standards. Act as Marketing Ops' primary liaison for regional field marketing. Explore new vendors on behalf of the team and take them through Procurement. Operating model and request intake Run the EMEA field marketing request intake: triage against priority tiers and SLAs, and route or decline work that doesn't fit the plan. Partner with marketing operations on behalf of field marketing to leverage use of AI automation. Design and maintain the localization workflow: translation tooling, a brand and terminology glossary, review routing, and vendor management. Translate global campaign strategy into modular playbooks and campaign kits that each region can adapt without rebuilding from scratch Budget, performance, and insight Manage and forecast the regional campaign budget, and allocate it across channels and programs for maximum ROI. Define regional KPIs (MQLs, cost per MQL, pipeline influence, revenue impact). Own reporting and attribution hygiene across regions, including data quality in Salesforce and HubSpot. Measure the operational impact of your work: hours returned to the team, request cycle time, and campaign activation speed. Bring local market feedback on competitors, customer needs, and emerging opportunities to Product Marketing, Global Campaigns, and leadership. Partner with the Senior Field Marketing Managers to align the operating model with pipeline goals. What you bring: Ability and/or willingness to use our product . 7+ years in B2B marketing, field marketing, or program operations, ideally in B2B software. You have a record of running integrated, pipeline-focused programs. Hands-on experience as a Senior Field Marketing Manager (or equivalent regional field marketing role) running events, account-based campaigns, and sales partnership. Strong hands-on skills in Salesforce and HubSpot (or a comparable CRM and marketing automation platform), including building campaigns and reporting on performance. Demonstrated experience building automations with workflow tools such as Claude and Zapier, or with scripting that connects systems. You know how to apply LLM tools to real operational work and where human review is required. Experience running multi-region programs, with an understanding of how regions and languages differ operationally. Strong program management: organized, detail-oriented, and comfortable juggling many programs, vendors, and stakeholders at once. A process-oriented, analytical mindset. You document what you build, measure what it does, and use data (A/B testing, attribution) to improve it. Excellent written and verbal English. You can influence sales leaders, AEs, and senior marketers, and present to executives. You are self-motivated, outcome-focused, and comfortable in a fast-paced, ambiguous environment. Experience supporting field marketing or sales organizations in EMEA (LATAM a plus). Experience managing budgets over €500K. Nice-to-haves: Experience with localization or translation management tools, or working with translation vendors. Fluency in a second European or Latin American language. Familiarity with ABM strategies and tools, and",
