    "summaryAr": "fal is the generative media ecosystem powering the next generation of AI products. We build the infrastructure, tools, and model access that teams need to move from idea to production, and do it at scale without compromise. For developers and enterprises, fal is the foundation that makes generative media not just possible, but practical: a unified platform where high-performance inference, orchestration, and observab",
    "descriptionAr": "fal is the generative media ecosystem powering the next generation of AI products. We build the infrastructure, tools, and model access that teams need to move from idea to production, and do it at scale without compromise. For developers and enterprises, fal is the foundation that makes generative media not just possible, but practical: a unified platform where high-performance inference, orchestration, and observability come together to unlock new categories of AI-native products. As generative media reshapes industries across a market projected to grow by hundreds of billions over the next decade, fal is becoming the ecosystem that ambitious teams build on. About this role: We're hiring an Accounting Operations Manager to own the operational core of fal's finance function: payables, spend management, procurement, and the books of our subsidiaries. You will work in Pacific Standard Time zone, run the weekly cadence that keeps vendors paid and spend under control, and you will turn the processes behind it into documented, audit-ready controls as fal completes its first financial statement audit and moves to a new ERP. This is a hands-on role for someone who likes building processes as much as running it. What you’ll do Spend management and AP oversight Own Ramp administration and allocate and oversee workload carried by offshore supporting AP team Act as the first point of contact for employee and vendor questions on spend, declined transactions, and payment status. Review card transactions and reimbursements for policy compliance, receipt support, GL coding, and accrual cut-off, and follow up on exceptions until they close. Run the weekly payables cycle end to end: invoice intake, matching to PO and receipt, GL and department coding, and approval routing. Maintain the vendor master, including W-9 collection, bank-detail changes verified by call-back, and controls against payment fraud. Prepare the weekly payment batch with a cash-requirements summary for finance leadership approval. Procurement and purchase orders Collaborate with Finance, Legal, and Ops on scalable procurement processes, including approval thresholds by amount, department, and vendor risk. Partner with Legal and budget owners so contracts, POs, and invoices tie out before payment. Subsidiary accounting and intercompany Keep the books for fal's subsidiaries under US GAAP, including journal entries, account reconciliations, and monthly close. Record, settle, and reconcile intercompany transactions and balances each month. Prepare elimination entries and support consolidation of entity financials. Bring acquired entities onto fal's chart of accounts, close calendar, and control environment. Audit readiness and systems Document process narratives and controls for AP, treasury, and procurement, and prepare the evidence auditors request. Help configure AP, procurement, and intercompany workflows in fal's new ERP. Use AI tools and automation to remove manual steps from invoice processing, coding, and reconciliations. 1099 reporting, tax and close support Own 1099 readiness year-round: vendor classification, TIN matching, and complete W-9 and W-8 files. Prepare, review, and approve annual 1099-NEC and 1099-MISC filings, and handle corrections and IRS notices. Support Tax function on ad hoc basis, including sales and use tax, and property tax. Support the month end close process, including but not limited to reconciliations of prepaids, deposits, payables, accruals. Qualifications/Nice-to-haves 5+ years in accounting operations, accounts payable, or general accounting Bachelor's degree in Accounting or Finance. Hands-on experience running AP and spend management in Ramp, Brex, or Bill.com , integrated with an ERP. Strong working knowledge of US GAAP, month-end close, and balance sheet reconciliations. Exposure to foreign subsidiaries, multi-currency accounting, or post-acquisition integration. Direct experience preparing and filing 1099s. A track record of designing internal controls: segregation of duties, approval matrices, and audit evidence. Precise and organized, and comfortable owning a recurring cadence with hard deadlines. Clear written communication with vendors, employees, and auditors. Fluency with AI tools and workflow automation to scale finance operations. Experience at a venture-backed, high-growth technology company, ideally through a first audit. CPA, or progress toward licensure. ERP implementation or migration experience (NetSuite, Rillet, or similar). What we offer at fal Interesting and challenging work A lot of learning and growth opportunities We offer visa sponsorship and will help you relocate to San Francisco. Health, dental, and vision insurance (US) Regular team events and offsites U.S. EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY INFORMATION: fal provides equal employment opportunities to applicants and employees without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, disability, or any other classification protected by applicable law. Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow",
