    "summaryAr": "GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster. The same principles built into our products are r",
    "descriptionAr": "GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster. The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. Co-create the future with us as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software. * Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab. An overview of this role As a Principal Executive Recruiter at GitLab, you’ll lead VP-level and other senior leadership searches across Engineering, Product, Security, IT, Data, and other technical teams. You’ll partner directly with senior executives to identify, engage, assess, and hire leaders, bringing market intelligence and a research-driven approach to complex, often confidential searches. Alongside owning searches end to end, you’ll help shape the strategies, frameworks, and practices that strengthen executive recruiting at GitLab, balancing search rigor with the agility of a fast-moving technology organization. What You’ll Do &nbsp;&nbsp; Lead VP-level and other senior leadership searches end to end, from search strategy and market mapping through assessment, selection, and closing. Advise C-suite executives and senior technical leaders on hiring decisions, challenge assumptions, and navigate complex stakeholder dynamics. Develop talent strategies using market mapping, competitive intelligence, creative sourcing, and recruiting data to guide each search. Build relationships with passive executive talent, understand their motivations, and connect opportunities to GitLab’s mission, technical vision, and business priorities. Partner with hiring leaders to define success profiles, assess executive capabilities and business impact, and guide evidence-based hiring decisions. Own executive candidate relationships and deliver a high-touch experience through compensation discussions, competing opportunities, and negotiations. Manage multiple confidential, business-critical searches with discretion, balancing urgency, quality, stakeholder alignment, and candidate experience. Collaborate with Talent Acquisition leadership and executive recruiting peers to improve search frameworks, assessment practices, reporting, and tools. What You’ll Bring&nbsp; Experience independently leading VP-level and senior executive searches through successful hires in an executive search firm, an in-house executive recruiting function, or both. Executive recruiting experience across technical functions such as Engineering, Product, Security, Data, or Infrastructure, with the technical fluency and curiosity to learn new domains. The ability to build trusted relationships with C-suite executives, influence senior stakeholders, and provide candid, evidence-based guidance on hiring decisions. Skills in talent research, market mapping, creative sourcing, leadership assessment, and engaging and closing passive executive talent. Business judgment, communication, and negotiation skills to navigate sensitive searches, complex compensation discussions, and competing executive priorities. Experience developing or improving executive search methodologies, frameworks, and processes while maintaining speed and flexibility. A hands-on approach to managing multiple high-priority searches independently and working through ambiguity. Experience in high-growth technology or enterprise software organizations, global executive searches, and distributed organizations is helpful. About the team You’ll join a globally distributed, remote-first Talent Acquisition team where clear communication and reliable follow-through matter. Guided by GitLab’s operating principles, including Speed with Quality, Ownership Mindset, and Customer Outcomes, we take ownership, move with urgency and rigor, and focus on hiring outcomes that matter to our internal customers. We share learnings and create reusable resources to continually improve the quality and consistency of hiring across Business teams. I changed the department lists in the overview and the “What you’ll bring” section, added “senior technical leaders” to the C-suite advising bullet, and added “technical vision” to the passive talent bullet. I also swapped “business acumen” for “technical fluency” since that’s the skill that matters most when assessing technical leaders. Everything else stays the same. If you’d like, I can also add language about assessing technical depth, such as architecture, engineering org design, or scaling teams, to the success profile bullet. The base salary range for this role’s listed level is currently for residents of the&nbsp;United States only. This range is intended to reflect the role's base salary rate in locations throughout the US.&nbsp;Grade level and salary ranges are determined through interviews and a review of education, experience, knowledge, skills, abilities of the applicant, equity with other team members, alignment with market data,&nbsp;and geographic location.&nbsp;The base salary range does not include any",
