    "summaryAr": "About the Role ClickHouse is hiring a Corporate Events Manager to own a portfolio of our biggest annual events from start to finish. These are the full-funnel programs that drive the global pipeline, move open opportunities forward and anchor our product launches. You’ll join a small, growing Corporate Events team and work with the broader GTM team alongside Product and Engineering. Your mix of programs will change a",
    "descriptionAr": "About the Role ClickHouse is hiring a Corporate Events Manager to own a portfolio of our biggest annual events from start to finish. These are the full-funnel programs that drive the global pipeline, move open opportunities forward and anchor our product launches. You’ll join a small, growing Corporate Events team and work with the broader GTM team alongside Product and Engineering. Your mix of programs will change as the calendar does. You’ll also package what works into kits that field marketers can rerun in their own markets, so no one starts from scratch. What You Will Be Doing Own a set of corporate programs end to end, from pre-event planning through on-site execution and post-event reporting. Examples include cloud partner events like Google Cloud Next and AWS re:Invent, RSA, and proprietary events like Open House Flagship and Open House Roadshows. Manage the full event lifecycle: contracts, vendors and agencies, agenda and content planning, staffing, logistics and on-the-ground delivery for booths, hosted events and activations. Run executive and customer meeting programs with Sales, SAs and Engineering: set booking targets, coordinate who is traveling in and invite clients. Support field marketers on registration, attendance targets, venues and agency onboarding when corporate programs travel. Work with the Demand Generation team on promotion, follow-up and attribution, so every event ties back to the pipeline. Stay flexible: pick up new programs and support teammates’ events as priorities shift across the calendar. What You Bring Along 4+ years of experience in corporate, field or event marketing in B2B SaaS. Preferred: experience in database, data analytics, cloud infrastructure or developer-focused companies. Proven track record running large-scale conferences, sponsored booths or hosted events, and managing several programs at once. Experience managing meeting programs and working closely with Sales on goals and follow-up. Excellent project management skills, with strong vendor, agency and budget management. Experience building repeatable playbooks, templates or kits that other teams can use. Analytical mindset, with the ability to measure event impact and report on it clearly. Ability to work independently in a fast-paced, remote-first environment, and comfort with ambiguity and shifting priorities. Travel required: 40% of the time, with heavier travel around peak event season. Perks Flexible work environment - ClickHouse is a globally distributed company and remote-friendly. We currently operate in over 25 countries. Healthcare - Employer contributions towards your healthcare. Equity in the company - Every new eligible team member who joins our company receives equity. Time off - Flexible time off in the US, generous entitlement in other countries. A USD$500 Home office setup if you’re a remote employee. Global Gatherings – We believe in the power of in-person connection and offer opportunities to engage with colleagues at company-wide offsites. Culture - We All Shape It As part of a rapidly scaling start-up, you will be instrumental in shaping our culture. Are you interested in finding out more about our culture? Learn more about our values here . Check out our blog posts or follow us on LinkedIn to find out more about what’s happening at ClickHouse. Equal Opportunity & Privacy ClickHouse provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type based on factors such as race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. Please see here for our Privacy Statement.",
