    "summaryAr": "This role is for one of our clients Compensation: $70 - $100 per hour Location: Remote – United Kingdom, Ireland, Germany, Spain, or Switzerland Employment Type: Full-Time Workload: Approximately 40 hours per week Compensation: Based on location and professional experience About the Role We are seeking an experienced FP&A Specialist to work with a leading AI company as part of its internal finance team. This role foc",
    "descriptionAr": "This role is for one of our clients Compensation: $70 - $100 per hour Location: Remote – United Kingdom, Ireland, Germany, Spain, or Switzerland Employment Type: Full-Time Workload: Approximately 40 hours per week Compensation: Based on location and professional experience About the Role We are seeking an experienced FP&A Specialist to work with a leading AI company as part of its internal finance team. This role focuses on core corporate finance activities, including financial planning, budgeting, forecasting, performance reporting, and business partnering. You will operate as an in-house finance professional, working closely with business leaders and functional teams to provide financial insights, support strategic decisions, and strengthen financial planning processes as the organisation continues to scale. This is a full-time, remote opportunity for finance professionals based in the United Kingdom, Ireland, Germany, Spain, or Switzerland. Requirements Key Responsibilities Develop, manage, and maintain annual budgets, financial forecasts, and multi-year financial plans. Conduct monthly and quarterly variance analysis, identifying key financial trends and explaining performance drivers to business stakeholders. Partner with cross-functional teams to support headcount planning, operational spending, resource allocation, and investment decisions. Build, maintain, and enhance financial models, dashboards, and management reporting frameworks. Support month-end closing activities and prepare financial reports for senior leadership. Translate financial data into actionable insights to support business planning and strategic decision-making. Identify opportunities to improve financial planning processes, reporting accuracy, and finance tools as the organisation grows. Required Qualifications & Skills 7+ years of experience in corporate finance, Financial Planning & Analysis (FP&A), or finance business partnering, primarily in an in-house environment. Previous experience working in technology companies, high-growth businesses, or similarly dynamic organisations is preferred. Proven ability to independently manage financial planning, budgeting, forecasting, and reporting responsibilities. Experience influencing senior stakeholders and collaborating with non-finance teams to drive business decisions. Strong financial modelling capabilities and advanced proficiency in Microsoft Excel or Google Sheets. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to explain financial concepts to non-finance stakeholders. Ability to work independently, manage competing priorities, and deliver accurate financial insights. Good-to-Have Skills Experience with financial planning and analysis platforms such as Anaplan, Adaptive Planning, or Pigment. Professional accounting or finance qualifications such as ACA, ACCA, CIMA, CPA, or CFA. Experience improving financial reporting systems, planning processes, and management dashboards. Important Candidate Criteria Senior individual contributors are encouraged to apply; a people-management title is not mandatory. Candidates should have substantial hands-on, in-house FP&A or corporate finance experience. Investment banking or private equity experience alone will not be considered sufficient for this role. English is the required working and interview language. Application Process Submit your updated resume. Complete a short screening form. Participate in a short AI interview, selecting FP&A or Finance Business Partnering as your domain. Engagement & Compensation The engagement structure, whether an independent contractor arrangement or employment through a local partner, will be confirmed during the hiring process. Compensation will be determined based on the candidate's location, experience, and professional expertise and discussed during the screening stage. Equal Opportunity All qualified applicants will be considered based on their relevant skills, experience, and professional qualifications, without unlawful discrimination under applicable local laws. Reasonable accommodations are available throughout the application process upon request. Find Jobs in Switzerland on Arbeitnow",
