    "summaryAr": "About Acodis Acodis is a Swiss software company based in Winterthur, providing AI-driven document processing for global Life Sciences companies. We help Quality and Regulatory teams move from document-centric to data-driven ways of working. The Mandate We are looking for an experienced freelance Product Manager to turn our AI platform into dedicated product solutions for two use cases. Working directly with managemen",
    "descriptionAr": "About Acodis Acodis is a Swiss software company based in Winterthur, providing AI-driven document processing for global Life Sciences companies. We help Quality and Regulatory teams move from document-centric to data-driven ways of working. The Mandate We are looking for an experienced freelance Product Manager to turn our AI platform into dedicated product solutions for two use cases. Working directly with management and our product engineering team, you will own both from discovery to market launch. Quality – Batch Record Review: AI-assisted review of executed batch records: checking completeness and correctness of entries, flagging deviations and GMP-relevant exceptions, and shortening review cycles ahead of batch disposition. Regulatory – CMC & Regulatory Submissions: Extraction and reuse of CMC data for submissions (CTD Module 3), consistency checks between source documents and submission content, and support for variations and post-approval changes. Mandate Deliverables Product definition & validation: Customer interviews, validated user workflows and value cases, and engineering-ready specifications and roadmap for both use cases. Pilot support: In our running pilots, including success criteria and a GxP-compliant validation approach. Go-to-market: Positioning, messaging, input and launch materials, together with the commercial team. Required Expertise 8+ years in product management or product consulting for digital, AI or enterprise software in Life Sciences. Hands-on expertise in batch record review and GMP manufacturing, or in CMC and regulatory submissions, with a solid understanding of GxP, data integrity and computerised system validation. Track record of taking products from concept to market, working independently on defined mandates. Nice to have: Experience with AI/LLM-based document processing, data pipelines, or platforms such as Veeva, MasterControl, Snowflake or Databricks. Mandate Details Duration & workload: 3–6 months from Jan/Feb 2027, 80–100%, extension possible. Location: Fully remote; no on-site presence in Winterthur required, but possible. Contract: Freelance (self-employed or via your own company) What We Offer A clearly scoped mandate with autonomy in how you deliver it. Direct access to management, engineering and customers, with short decision paths. The chance to shape two flagship products, with potential for a follow-on mandate. How to Apply Please upload your CV and relevant references, availability and daily rate to our recruiting platform. Find Jobs in Switzerland on Arbeitnow",
