    "summaryAr": "About the Team OpenAI’s mission is to build safe artificial general intelligence (AGI) which benefits all of humanity. This long-term undertaking brings the world’s best scientists, engineers, and business professionals into one lab together to accomplish this. The GTM Agentic Workflows team is building OpenAI’s agentic go-to-market operating system. We work with sellers, GTM leaders, and partners in GTM Systems, Dat",
    "descriptionAr": "About the Team OpenAI’s mission is to build safe artificial general intelligence (AGI) which benefits all of humanity. This long-term undertaking brings the world’s best scientists, engineers, and business professionals into one lab together to accomplish this. The GTM Agentic Workflows team is building OpenAI’s agentic go-to-market operating system. We work with sellers, GTM leaders, and partners in GTM Systems, Data Science, and Product to connect customer intelligence to account strategy, helping teams prioritize opportunities, grow adoption across accounts, and spend time where it matters most. About the Role As an individual contributor on the GTM Agentic Workflows team, you’ll own the design, rollout, and performance of processes and workflows across the customer lifecycle, from lead routing through deal execution, delivery, and consumption. Orchestration is central to this role. You’ll bring sellers, GTM leaders, and cross-functional partners together around a shared outcome, then connect the work of people, systems, and agentic workflows to deliver it. In this role, you will: Prioritize problems with GTM leaders and the field. Look at where sellers repeat work, where deals stall, and which handoffs break down. Use the frequency and impact of those problems to decide what to tackle first. Strengthen the foundations of GTM workflows. Set the strategy for enriching person and company data, and partner with GTM Systems on lead routing and how sellers manage accounts and opportunities in Salesforce. Orchestrate delivery across teams. Align owners on the outcome, sequence work across functions, and resolve competing priorities. Make clear who decides, what information carries forward, and when the next team can act. Design and launch workflows with Product and Enterprise Systems. Define what triggers the workflow, what information an agent needs, and when a person should review or approve an action. Pilot with field teams and partner with Enablement on rollout. Own performance after launch. Measure adoption alongside outcomes such as lead response time, accuracy of proposed updates, and time to complete a handoff. Use those results and field feedback to decide what to improve next. You might thrive in this role if you have: 8+ years of experience in Sales Operations, Revenue Operations, or related roles at a high-growth technology company Strong systems thinking with deep experience designing and scaling sales systems, processes, and workflows across the full sales lifecycle Experience taking a multi-step GTM workflow from a field problem through rollout. You can explain what you automated, where people retained judgment, and how you measured whether it worked. Strong proficiency in Salesforce and data tools (e.g., SQL, Excel). Strong analytical skills with high attention to detail Experience with territory design, account structures, and pipeline management A track record of leading through influence. You can point to a cross-functional initiative where you brought teams with competing priorities to a decision and saw it through to delivery. Ability to operate in ambiguity, prioritize effectively, and manage multiple high-impact initiatives simultaneously About OpenAI OpenAI is an AI research and deployment company dedicated to ensuring that general-purpose artificial intelligence benefits all of humanity. We push the boundaries of the capabilities of AI systems and seek to safely deploy them to the world through our products. AI is an extremely powerful tool that must be created with safety and human needs at its core, and to achieve our mission, we must encompass and value the many different perspectives, voices, and experiences that form the full spectrum of humanity. We are an equal opportunity employer, and we do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability, genetic information, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. For additional information, please see OpenAI’s Affirmative Action and Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement . Background checks for applicants will be administered in accordance with applicable law, and qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment consistent with those laws, including the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers, and the California Fair Chance Act, for US-based candidates. For unincorporated Los Angeles County workers: we reasonably believe that criminal history may have a direct, adverse and negative relationship with the following job duties, potentially resulting in the withdrawal of a conditional offer of employment: protect computer hardware entrusted to you from theft, loss or damage; return all computer hardware in your possession (including the data contained therein) upon termination of employment or end of assignment; and maintain the confidentiality of proprietary, confidential, and non-public information. In addition, job duties require access to secure and protected information technology systems and related data security obligations. To notify OpenAI that you believe this job posting is non-compliant, please submit a report through this form . No response will be provided to inquiries unrelated to job posting compliance. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities, and requests can be made via this link . OpenAI Global Applicant Privacy Policy At OpenAI, we believe artificial intelligence has the potential to help people solve immense global challenges, and we want the upside of AI to be widely shared. Join us in shaping the future of technology.",
