    "summaryAr": "Grafana Labs is the company behind Grafana Cloud, the fully managed observability platform trusted by more than 10,000 organizations to ensure reliability, resolve incidents faster, and optimize telemetry at scale. Built on open source and open standards and designed for interoperability across any stack, Grafana Cloud brings AI to observability and observability to AI, giving teams (and their agents) unified visibil",
    "descriptionAr": "Grafana Labs is the company behind Grafana Cloud, the fully managed observability platform trusted by more than 10,000 organizations to ensure reliability, resolve incidents faster, and optimize telemetry at scale. Built on open source and open standards and designed for interoperability across any stack, Grafana Cloud brings AI to observability and observability to AI, giving teams (and their agents) unified visibility so they can see, understand, and act on all their disparate data, wherever it lives, and move at the speed of their ambitions. Customers, including Anthropic, Bloomberg, NVIDIA, Microsoft, and Salesforce, rely on Grafana Labs. We are a 100% remote company with team members across 40+ countries, backed by leading investors including Lightspeed Venture Partners, Sequoia Capital, GIC, Coatue, J.P. Morgan, CapitalG, and Lead Edge Capital. Learn more at grafana.com and follow us on LinkedIn and X . We’re scaling fast and staying true to what makes us different: an open-source legacy, a global collaborative culture, and a passion for meaningful work. Our team thrives in an innovation-driven environment where transparency, autonomy, and trust fuel everything we do. You may not meet every requirement, and that’s okay. If this role excites you, we’d love you to raise your hand for what could be a truly career-defining opportunity. The Opportunity We’re looking for a Director of Sales Talent Acquisition to lead our global team of sales recruiters and make sales hiring a genuine competitive advantage for Grafana Labs. You will set the direction for how we attract, assess and hire the sellers who drive our growth, and you will do it as a core member of the sales organization, not a service function that sits beside it. You’ll work hand in hand with senior sales leaders, RevOps, Finance and the wider People team to turn hiring plans into predictable outcomes. This is a leader who is energized by data, spots risks to hiring goals before they land, and turns insight into innovative, AI-powered tools that help the business make faster, better decisions. If you have built and rolled out ICP-based hiring and want to do it at global scale in a fast-growing, remote-first company, this is your role. What you'll be doing Lead, coach and develop a global team of sales recruiters and sourcers, setting a clear strategy, high standards and a culture of ownership across regions. Be highly data driven: build a rigorous view of pipeline, funnel conversion, time to hire and capacity against hiring plans, and flag risks to hiring goals early so the business can act before targets are missed. Plan effectively and remove surprises: build forward-looking hiring plans with sales leaders, RevOps and Finance, surface dependencies and trade-offs early, and keep stakeholders informed so there are no unwelcome surprises. Set a high bar for the team and yourself, driving performance against ambitious hiring targets and consistently hitting and exceeding them. Lead from the front and stay close to the work: step into key searches, candidate conversations and closes when it matters, and put the team’s success ahead of your own profile. Turn insights and data into innovative, AI-based dashboards and tools that give sales leaders, RevOps and Finance real-time visibility and help the team work smarter. Build strong, trusted partnerships with senior sales leaders, RevOps, Finance and other business stakeholders, becoming their go-to adviser on talent strategy, headcount planning and market conditions. Position Sales TA as an integral part of the sales team, aligned to its goals, planning cycles and rhythms, and accountable for shared outcomes. Define and roll out ICP-based hiring for sales roles, so that every search is anchored in a clear, evidence-based picture of what great looks like at Grafana. Build an always-on sales talent pipeline: work with sourcers and use CRM tools to run nurture campaigns that keep future sellers warm, so the team is never starting from zero when a role opens. Collaborate closely with the wider People team, including Talent Team peers, People Ops, Compensation and Total Rewards, to deliver a consistent, high-quality candidate and hiring manager experience. Own the sales hiring process and tooling, including Greenhouse, ensuring data quality, process adherence and continuous improvement across the team. Champion the Grafana Labs employer brand in the sales talent market, with a focus on engaging both passive and active candidates globally. What makes you a great fit 3+ years leading a Talent Acquisition team, ideally in a global tech sales capacity. A deep understanding of what makes a great software sales professional, and how to assess for it across segments, regions and seniority levels. Strong evidence of using data and AI to solve hiring problems, including building dashboards or tools that changed how a business made hiring decisions. Evidence of implementing and rolling out ICP-based hiring. Experience using sourcers and recruiting CRM tools to build nurture campaigns and an always-on pipeline of sales talent. A competitive, goal-driven mindset: you thrive on a high bar, set ambitious targets for yourself and your team, and have a track record of hitting and exceeding them. Excellent planning skills, with the ability to anticipate dependencies, build realistic hiring plans and remove surprises for the business before they happen. A leader who rolls up their sleeves: you are happy to get stuck into a critical search, a candidate close or a messy process problem alongside the team, you share credit freely, and you care far more about the result than about who gets the recognition. A track record of partnering credibly with senior sales leaders, RevOps and Finance, and of earning a seat at the table. A collaborative mindset, with an understanding that success is not possible without being part of a wider People team. Comfort in a high-paced environment, where you embrace change and amb",
