    "summaryAr": "About Ramp Ramp is building the smart infrastructure for finance teams, embedded in the transaction flow of every dollar a business spends. We automate how over $275B in annualized spend flows in and out of 85,000+ companies: authorizing payments, flagging risk, categorizing spend, and closing books. The problems are high-stakes, data-dense, and unforgiving. We hire people with high agency and high urgency. We look f",
    "descriptionAr": "About Ramp Ramp is building the smart infrastructure for finance teams, embedded in the transaction flow of every dollar a business spends. We automate how over $275B in annualized spend flows in and out of 85,000+ companies: authorizing payments, flagging risk, categorizing spend, and closing books. The problems are high-stakes, data-dense, and unforgiving. We hire people with high agency and high urgency. We look for slope over intercept. We care less about where you trained and more about what you’ve built. At Ramp, everyone is a builder who owns problems end to end and makes consequential decisions that shape the outcome. The median Ramp customer saves 7.5% and grows revenue 16% in their first year – far in excess of businesses operating without Ramp. We believe every ambitious company deserves the same. If you want to build systems that directly shape how companies move and manage billions, Ramp is the place to do it. About the role Ramp Stack brings AI to the accounting work that happens after the transaction: reconciliations, prepaids and amortization, fixed assets, payroll entries, accruals, allocations, and variance analysis. Stack prepares reviewable work so the customer's team keeps accounting judgment and approval. As a Stack Account Executive, you'll sell to finance and accounting leaders (Controllers, VPs of Accounting, CFOs) in a new, fast-moving product motion. You'll hear how a team actually closes the books, find the recurring manual step that creates drag, and turn it into a focused proof path and a commercial plan. This is broader than a month-end close pitch: you'll connect Stack to the finance team's goals for cleaner data, fewer handoffs, faster close, and more confidence in reporting. What you'll do Own the full sales cycle from first conversation to signed contract: discovery, tailored demo or scoped pilot, business case, negotiation, close. Run workflow-level discovery: identify the recurring task, its inputs, the preparer and reviewer, and the cost of keeping it manual. Scope and run pilots against a baseline and a success metric, then convert them into a mutual action plan and a decision. Run a high-ownership, high-velocity motion (10–15 deals a month discussed as the lower band; quota target to confirm). Combine Stack with Ramp's core products where it genuinely improves the data, control, or handoff behind the workflow. Bring field feedback to Product, Marketing, and Enablement while the motion is still being built. What you need Quota-carrying, full-cycle closing experience selling to finance or accounting buyers (years of experience to confirm). Exposure to accounting workflows (for example from Basis, FloQast, NetSuite, or similar reporting, forecasting, or close tools). Comfort with a high-ownership, high-velocity motion in an early product. Proven high agency: you build your own pipeline and process without waiting for a playbook. Ability to discuss close, reconciliation, and reporting workflows credibly with Controllers and CFOs. Daily, practical use of AI in your own work. Nice to have CPA, or an accounting or finance background, even earlier in your career. An accounting-to-sales transition, or relationship-manager experience with sales, negotiation, and upsell or cross-sell. Experience on a NetSuite incubation team or with a reporting or forecasting tool. Benefits available to all full-time Ramp employees (Global) Flexible PTO Centralized home-office equipment ordering Health and wellness stipend Budget for intra-office travel Weekly coffee stipend United States 100% medical, dental & vision insurance coverage for you, with partial coverage for dependents One Medical annual membership 401(k), including employer match on contributions made while employed by Ramp Fertility HRA (up to $10,000 per year) Parental leave: up to 16 weeks (birthing + bonding) or 8 weeks (bonding only) at 100% pay Pet insurance In-office perks: lunch, snacks, drinks, and more Relocation expense coverage to NYC or SF (if needed) Canada Group medical, dental, and vision coverage through Sun Life Life, AD&D, and disability coverage Fertility drug coverage (up to $4,000 lifetime) Group Retirement Plan with employer match (RRSP + DPSP) Parental leave: up to 16 weeks (birthing + bonding) or 8 weeks (bonding only) at 100% pay, with additional time available at reduced pay Employee Assistance Program and virtual care through Lumino Health United Kingdom Private medical insurance through Freedom Elite Virtual GP and at-home care via eMed x Livi Workplace pension through Penfold, with salary sacrifice option Parental leave: up to 16 weeks (birthing + bonding) or 8 weeks (bonding only) at 100% pay with additional time available at reduced pay Referral Instructions If you are being referred for the role, please contact that person to apply on your behalf. Other notices Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records. Beware of recruiting scams: Ramp will only contact you through official @ Ramp.com email addresses and will never ask for payment or sensitive personal information during the hiring process. Ramp Applicant Privacy Notice",
