    "summaryAr": "The Learning Team at ClickHouse is growing fast as more users discover its power and need to understand how to use it effectively. We deliver training in many formats, including on-demand at ClickHouse Academy; live training delivered online via Zoom; in-person training for customers; and training at community events and conferences. We also have a credential and certification program to complement our training cours",
    "descriptionAr": "The Learning Team at ClickHouse is growing fast as more users discover its power and need to understand how to use it effectively. We deliver training in many formats, including on-demand at ClickHouse Academy; live training delivered online via Zoom; in-person training for customers; and training at community events and conferences. We also have a credential and certification program to complement our training courses and recognize those individuals who are ClickHouse subject matter experts. You will be responsible for delivering engaging and effective training to our users, customers, and partners. Courses vary from 60-minute onboarding and fundamentals training to multi-day deep dives. What you will be doing: Here is a list of the typical tasks you would be performing as a ClickHouse Instructor: Becoming a ClickHouse SME Teaching ClickHouse courses both virtually and in person for public and private deliveries Assisting the curriculum development team in the design and review of current and new courses Assisting the certification team with the design and development of certification exams Traveling to Meetups, conferences, and customer sites to deliver training and promote ClickHouse to the community Travel is expected and a typical part of the job Requirements: At least 5 years of proven experience as an instructor in the world of database management and distributed systems A self-motivated attitude that provides you with the desire and determination to become a Subject Matter Expert in ClickHouse Ability to learn new technologies quickly and effectively Expert knowledge of SQL Proven experience and ability to teach to audiences of all different sizes and backgrounds Ability to travel up to 40% of the time Excellent communication skills Technical breadth and depth in relevant subjects such as DBMS, OLAP, Cloud/SaaS platforms, distributed systems, and software engineering You have a high level of responsibility, ownership, and accountability Bonus points: Experience teaching OLAP database systems Experience with ClickHouse database Being a ClickHouse Certified Developer Experience with one or more Cloud Service Providers such as AWS, GCP, Azure Ability to work cross-functionally amongst engineering, support, product and development teams Technical degree (e.g. Computer Science or related field) You'll love this role if: You have excellent communication skills and thrive in a customer-facing role You are self-driven, curious, and eager to continuously learn and grow. You possess a mindset of teamwork, global engagement, empathy, and a drive for solving challenging problems. You have a sense of adventure and urgency in building the most scalable, highest-performing, largest, and fastest databases in the world. Perks Flexible work environment - ClickHouse is a globally distributed company and remote-friendly. We currently operate in over 25 countries. Healthcare - Employer contributions towards your healthcare. Equity in the company - Every new eligible team member who joins our company receives equity. Time off - Flexible time off in the US, generous entitlement in other countries. A USD$500 Home office setup if you’re a remote employee. Global Gatherings – We believe in the power of in-person connection and offer opportunities to engage with colleagues at company-wide offsites. Culture - We All Shape It As part of a rapidly scaling start-up, you will be instrumental in shaping our culture. Are you interested in finding out more about our culture? Learn more about our values here . Check out our blog posts or follow us on LinkedIn to find out more about what’s happening at ClickHouse. Equal Opportunity & Privacy ClickHouse provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type based on factors such as race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. Please see here for our Privacy Statement.",
