    "summaryAr": "Replit is the agentic software creation platform that enables anyone to build applications using natural language. With millions of users worldwide, Replit is democratizing software development by removing traditional barriers to application creation. About the role Connectors let Replit’s agents and applications securely access the tools and data people already use. Behind every connection are hard systems problems:",
    "descriptionAr": "Replit is the agentic software creation platform that enables anyone to build applications using natural language. With millions of users worldwide, Replit is democratizing software development by removing traditional barriers to application creation. About the role Connectors let Replit’s agents and applications securely access the tools and data people already use. Behind every connection are hard systems problems: whose identity is being used, what they’re allowed to access, how credentials stay valid, and how those guarantees hold across services and execution environments. We’re looking for a Senior or Staff Software Engineer with deep experience in authentication, authorization, security, and distributed systems to own this foundation. You’ll build and operate the infrastructure that makes connections work reliably across Replit’s projects, agent conversations, and environment builds. This is a hands-on engineering role, not a security advisory position or a job focused on adding individual integrations. You’ll trace behavior across service boundaries, make architectural decisions, ship production changes, and simplify an evolving platform. Success means connections are secure and reliable end to end, and the team can confidently build on the systems you own. You will Own authentication and authorization across the connection lifecycle. Design how users, agents, applications, and services establish identity, receive access, and act on behalf of others. Build reliable credential infrastructure. Handle OAuth flows, token refresh, revocation, reauthorization, and secure credential storage, including concurrency and partial failures. Make connections work across the platform. Follow requests through application services, credential proxies, agent execution, and environment builds, preserving security guarantees at every boundary. Design and operate distributed systems. Improve service-to-service communication, tenant isolation, failure recovery, and observability across shared and isolated deployments. Handle provider-specific constraints without compromising the platform. Account for differences such as user versus bot credentials, token limits, and source-control authentication. Lead safe migrations and reduce technical debt. Replace fragile or duplicated paths with clearer ownership and simpler designs while keeping existing customer workflows working. Raise the team’s technical judgment. Explain system behavior clearly, lead design discussions, mentor engineers, and partner with security, infrastructure, and product teams. Examples of what you could do Fix a token-refresh race that causes connections to fail when multiple services use them concurrently. Trace an authorization failure from an agent request through the credential proxy to the provider, then address the underlying design problem. Design a connection lifecycle that behaves consistently across projects, conversations, and environment builds. Migrate customers to a stronger identity and authorization model without disrupting their applications. Remove legacy connection paths and add end-to-end tests that make future changes safer. Required skills and experience Deep hands-on experience with authentication and authorization systems, including OAuth 2.0, access scopes, credential lifecycles, and trust boundaries. Strong distributed systems fundamentals, including concurrency, consistency, retries, idempotency, and partial failure. Experience designing, shipping, and operating production backend infrastructure with meaningful security and reliability requirements. Ability to understand an unfamiliar system end to end and debug failures across multiple services and third-party APIs. A track record of owning complex changes through design, implementation, rollout, and production validation. Pragmatic engineering judgment: you improve existing systems incrementally, reduce unnecessary complexity, and know when a provider-specific exception is justified. Clear technical communication and a willingness to help other engineers develop deeper systems understanding. Preferred qualifications Experience with service identity, delegated access, token federation, or credential-management infrastructure. Experience with multi-tenant isolation, enterprise governance, or customer-managed cloud deployments. Experience migrating authentication or authorization systems while preserving existing customer access. Experience leading cross-team architectural work and mentoring engineers. Bonus points Familiarity with emerging cross-app access standards such as Cross-App Access (XAA), as well as OAuth 2.0 token exchange, OpenID Connect, and identity federation. Experience designing developer-facing APIs, SDKs, or connector-authoring tools. Familiarity with AI agent tool execution or Model Context Protocol (MCP). Experience supporting integrations with complex authentication behavior, including collaboration tools and source-control providers. Location This is a full-time role that can be held from our Foster City, CA office. The role has an in-office requirement of Monday, Wednesday, and Friday. Full-Time Employee Benefits Include: 💰 Competitive Salary & Equity 💹 401(k) Program with a 4% match ( US Only ) ⚕️ Health, Dental, Vision and Life Insurance 🩼 Short Term and Long Term Disability 🚼 Paid Parental, Medical, Caregiver Leave 🏝 Flexible Time Off (FTO) + Holidays 🚗 Commuter Benefits ( In-Office & US Only ) 📱 Monthly Wellness Stipend 🧑‍💻 Autonomous Work Environment 🖥 In Office Set-Up Reimbursement ( In-Office Only ) 🚀 Quarterly Team Gatherings ☕ In Office Amenities ( In-Office Only ) Want to learn more about what we are up to? Self-driving Company Replit Agent at Scale AI Adoption Build Open-Source Apps Interviewing + Culture at Replit Operating Principles Reasons not to work at Replit To achieve our mission of making programming more accessible around the world, we need our team to be representative of the world. We welcome your uniqu",
